LATENT DISPATCH
Fri Sep 11 · 5 items · ~4 min

FERRITE-70B IS HERE
Ferrite released the 70B this morning under Apache 2.0. First-day numbers from our harness: it beats every other open model we track on structured extraction and tool use, and lands between the mid-tier proprietary models on reasoning. It needs two 80GB cards or a hosted provider; Kestrel and Argent both say "next week." Full benchmark table Monday. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/ferrite-70b

AGENTS VS. WORKFLOWS: A TAXONOMY THAT ACTUALLY HELPS
A long post from the Larkspur team distinguishing workflows (fixed steps, model calls inside them) from agents (the model picks the steps). Their claim: 80% of production "agents" are workflows and would be more reliable if built as such. We agree. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/agents-vs-workflows

SEPTEMBER PRICE TRACKER PREVIEW
Halfway through the month, mid-tier prices are down another 20% after the Argent/Nimbus/Kestrel round. Frontier flat again. Open-weights hosting is the new battleground; expect Ferrite-70B pricing to set the floor.

SABLE LABS RAISES
$1.2B at a valuation we will not repeat because it will be wrong by the time you read this. Use of funds: compute. Always compute.

SHORT TAKES
· Quillon-M now handles multi-page documents as a single call.
· Nimbus adds SOC 2 Type II to its trust page.
· A clear guide to per-tenant cost attribution when everything runs through one API key: https://latentdispatch.ai/p/tenant-cost

